  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy [--base main]` is a new gate tier. It maps the diff to the release `--ignored` heavy lanes that the diff reaches. It runs only those lanes.\n- The reach follows the dependencies between our crates. The planner reads them from `crates/*/Cargo.toml`. A source change in `motion` reaches the heavy lanes of `motion` and `app`.\n- A changed suite file reaches its own heavy binary only. Shared test code reaches the heavy lanes of its crate. A workspace manifest change reaches each heavy lane.\n- A post script, machine file, catalog case or fixture reaches the heavy binaries that read it. The planner uses the mappers of the quick tier for this.\n- The steps are the heavy steps of the release tier, with the same names and commands. `--only`, `--failed` and `--dry-run` work.\n- `plan::heavy_steps` now calls `plan::heavy_steps_where` with a filter that keeps all targets. The release plan does not change.\n- `main.rs` has one function, `changed_since`, for the diff of the quick tier and the heavy tier.\n- AGENTS.md has the new rule **Heavy lanes at review**. A PR that reaches a heavy lane is not ready while a reached heavy test is red or not run. The review comment lists the heavy lanes that ran.\n- The `gate` skill, the `work-issue` skill and the `PR-reviewer` agent have the matching steps.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe quick tier selects test binaries by Gate map and does not run `--ignored` tests. Only the cut ran each heavy lane. No command mapped a diff to the heavy lanes that it reaches through the crate dependencies.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins, all in `xtask/src/heavy_plan_tests.rs`:\n\n- `gate_heavy_is_a_tier_with_a_base`\n- `reach_follows_the_crate_dependencies`\n- `a_motion_source_change_reaches_the_motion_and_app_heavy_lanes`\n- `a_changed_suite_reaches_only_its_own_heavy_binary`\n- `shared_test_code_reaches_the_heavy_lanes_of_its_own_crate_only`\n- `a_kernel_or_workspace_change_reaches_every_heavy_lane`\n- `a_diff_outside_the_heavy_crates_reaches_no_heavy_lane`\n- `a_catalog_case_reaches_the_binary_that_reads_it`\n- `an_unreadable_manifest_is_an_error_not_a_smaller_plan`\n\nRed before the fix: `gate_heavy_is_a_tier_with_a_base` failed on unchanged code with `unknown tier 'heavy' (quick | batch | release | test)`. The other pins need the new module.\n\nMutation results:\n\n- The tier `heavy` removed from `parse_gate`: `gate_heavy_is_a_tier_with_a_base` is red. Restored: green.\n- The dependency reach removed in `heavy::reached` (own crate only): `a_motion_source_change_reaches_the_motion_and_app_heavy_lanes` and `a_kernel_or_workspace_change_reaches_every_heavy_lane` are red. Restored: green.\n- The target filter removed in `plan::heavy_steps_where`: five pins are red (suite, shared test code, motion, no-reach, kernel or workspace). Restored: green.\n\nGate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` is green (`xtask unit tests`, 1 step, 0 failed). `cargo clippy -p xtask --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n`cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main --dry-run` on this branch prints \"the diff reaches no heavy lane: nothing to run\". This PR changes no crate with heavy lanes.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No heavy step ran in release through the new tier. The pins compare the planned steps with the steps of the release tier.\n- `pr-test.yml` does not run the heavy tier. This PR does not change `.github/`. That workflow also refuses a PR that changes `xtask/`. This part of the issue stays open for the maintainer.\n- The wrappers `scripts/gate.sh` and `scripts/gate.ps1` do not forward `heavy`. Use `cargo xtask gate heavy`.\n- The heavy tier runs its steps one at a time. It does not use the shared lanes of the release executor.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone. No open PR changes these files.\n\nDecision: `docs/decisions/2568-gate-heavy-diff.md`.\n\nProcess change: yes\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #2568\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
